  "notes" : "Volim Mail 1.0 Build 133 — scheduled sends now go out exactly once.\n\nMail:\n- A scheduled message is marked as sending before it leaves and as sent the moment Gmail accepts it, so it can never be delivered twice; a failure after delivery is logged instead of retried.\n- A send that Gmail rejected before delivery retries a few times with growing delays, then stops and is shown as failed with a Send Now button; anything uncertain is shown as \"may have been sent, check your Sent mailbox\" and never resent automatically.\n- Sending no longer reports failure when only the follow-up details request fails after a successful delivery.\n\nTesting note: every Pro feature is unlocked in this build and the upgrade prompt is disabled.\n\nThis early-access build is signed with the existing Apple Development identity and a separately signed update manifest. It is not notarized. Apple Developer ID distribution is deferred; first-time installation may require normal macOS approval. Existing installations use the signed GitHub update feed.\n\nThe update preserves existing mail data and settings.",
